import R4Common

/-! # BF 2025: Capital (P3-P7; generated by R4/tools/gen_pkgs.py from specs/pkgs/bf.json)

IRCM on dividends and other income from securities (12,5 %) (CGI 2023 art. 140 2) (edition at 2023; LF 2024 and LFR 2024 checked: art. 140 not amended; LF 2025 not held)): art. 140 2): income from securities (valeurs mobilières) 12,5 %, bonds issued in Burkina Faso 6 %; art. 141: half rate for the first three years of new companies.

IRCM on interest on deposit and current accounts (25 % halved: 12,5 %) (CGI 2023 art. 140 1) (edition at 2023; LF 2024/LFR 2024 checked; LF 2025 not held)): art. 140 1): income from claims (créances) 25 %, halved for interest on deposit and current accounts with banks, financial institutions, the Treasury and agricultural credit funds (art. 129); the household's interest is taken to be bank deposit interest.

Impôt sur les revenus fonciers (18 % / 25 % on monthly rent after a 50 % abatement) (CGI 2023 art. 125-126 (edition at 2023; LF 2024/LFR 2024 checked; LF 2025 not held)): art. 125: net income = gross rent of the month or period less a flat 50 % abatement; art. 126: progressive bands 0-100 000 F 18 %, above 25 %. The household's annual rent is taken as twelve equal monthly rents.

Taxe sur les plus-values immobilières (10 % of the gain) (CGI 2023 art. 161-166 (edition at 2023; LF 2024/LFR 2024 checked; LF 2025 not held)): art. 166: the tax rate is 10 %; the gain is the sale price less the acquisition price and costs (art. 164-165). -/

namespace BfGlobal
open TaxKernel TaxKernel.Global

def ircmDiv : Family :=
